label_alpha_what.SetOrder(2)
palette.SetAlphaReadout(@label_alpha_num)
palette.AddAlphaDelta(@label_alpha_top, 5.0)
palette.AddAlphaDelta(@label_alpha_bot, -5.0)

# ── nothing here, and that is the change ─────────────────────────────────────
#
# Click-and-hold on any +/- keeps stepping, and nothing in this page ticks while
# a button is held still. This used to need a node -- a drawable that drew
# nothing, spawned into the bar so the compose walk would visit it and it could
# tick the palette from inside its own DrawInto. The palette now claims Animated
# (ontology/Animated.h) and is stepped by whatever drives that family, so the
# relation is stated on the palette instead of smuggled through a child of the
# thing it steps. A script that wants the repeat spawns nothing.
